/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 53 0 R
/T (Explanation. The MAE of 0.50 means predictions are off by about half a quality point on average. The RMSE of 0.62 is a little larger because it penalises big errors more. R2 = 0.40 means the model explains only about 40% of the variation in quality of unseen wines; 60% is unexplained. Always predicting the training mean would give an RMSE of 0.81, so the model is better than guessing but not by a large margin. Train R2 \(0.35\) is slightly below test R2, so there is no sign of overfitting; the test split was probably a little easier, so a single split should not be over-trusted. On a scale where scores are mostly 5 or 6, an error of half a point is substantial.)
/E (Explanation. The MAE of 0.50 means predictions are off by about half a quality point on average. The RMSE of 0.62 is a little larger because it penalises big errors more. R2 = 0.40 means the model explains only about 40% of the variation in quality of unseen wines; 60% is unexplained. Always predicting the training mean would give an RMSE of 0.81, so the model is better than guessing but not by a large margin. Train R2 \(0.35\) is slightly below test R2, so there is no sign of overfitting; the test split was probably a little easier, so a single split should not be over-trusted. On a scale where scores are mostly 5 or 6, an error of half a point is substantial.)
